Z||000005||JohnsFiero||09-10-2000||09:22 PM||||I called PM Cares for the recalls on my '84 and was told that their computers don't go back more than 10 years.  Was told to call a Pontiac dealer for the information because their database goes back further...or is it farther?!<P>John    ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||09-10-2000||09:42 PM||||Spell check likes both of them and I'm too lazy to go get a dictionary.  If I had to guess, I would say "farther", but who knows.||||reg||1
Z||000007||jmw||09-11-2000||06:03 PM||||1-800-PMCARES can tell you what recalls were ISSUED for your car, but NOT whether the work was done. Dealers ALSO do not have that info. Basically the answer I got was that NO ONE keeps that info except the owner(s) of the car. PMCARES told me what recalls were issued for mine and said to take it a Pontiac dealer. They said the dealer may charge me a diagnostic fee if they have to take anything apart in order to determine whether the work was done, which I think is sort of bogus, because in my mind it should be free, but anyway, that's what I was told. I know for the engine fire deal they placed a gold 2" x 3" sticker in the interior trunklid. There were 3 other recalls on my '84, but that's the only evidence I can find of recall work [the others were for rear brakes, maintenance, and engine splash shield].  If you take yours to a dealer, please let me know how it goes. I need to take mine too, just to be on the safe side. Good luck!||||reg||7
